Peter, Juri, Ingo, Vincent,

Sashiko [1] reported that rcu_dereference() was being called outside an
explicit RCU read-side critical section under CONFIG_PROVE_RCU. The next
iteration will update call sites across kernel/sched/fair.c to use
rcu_dereference_sched() and covers the remaining lockless readers that were
missed during the initial migration. Also, since rd is annotated as __rcu,
several untouched direct dereferences triggered Sparse "dereference of noderef
expression" warnings (i.e., make C=2 kernel/sched/).
I will be sure to resolve these too.

